<title>FRANCE: Paribas sees 600 mln Ffr cap gain on Nord.</title>
<headline>Paribas sees 600 mln Ffr cap gain on Nord.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French holding company Cie Financiere de Paribas said on Thursday that it would make a 600 million franc capital gain from the sale of its Credit du Nord retail banking unit to Societe Generale.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said Credit du Nord is valued at a net 1.6 billion in Paribas' accounts, while the initial agreement on the sale of the unit to Societe Generale is for 2.2 billion francs.</p>
<p>Paribas Societe Generale said earlier on Thursday they approved the start of talks aimed at reaching a fast agreement on the sale of Credit du Nord by Paribas to Societe Generale for 2.2 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
